0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                             ;  B8Script interpreter for the Z80
0000                             ;  Spec: docs/b8script.md (2026-11-21).
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Three switches, set in the EQU lines below:
0000                             ;    CPM      0 = generic ROM build (KEY/CONOUT at fixed addresses)
0000                             ;             1 = CP/M 2.2 .COM file: loads the file named on the command line
0000                             ;    EDITOR   1 = with the line editor built in (see the end of this file):
0000                             ;                 the spec's suggested standard. It goes with either setting
0000                             ;                 of the other two.
0000                             ;    CHECKED  0 = no checks (spec: the programmer is responsible)
0000                             ;             1 = starts with every variable at 0 and every word undefined,
0000                             ;                 and stops on every error in the spec's table (and Ctrl-C)
0000                             ;                 with a four-line report: the letter and the place as line
0000                             ;                 and column, the text there, and both stacks. See `error`.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  In every build Ctrl-C stops a running program (an unchecked build stops
0000                             ;  without a word): see the console layer for the rules, the held key and
0000                             ;  the break-off cell.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Assembler: asm80 (https://maly.github.io/asm80-node/), Z80 mode.
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                CPM:      EQU   0   ; 1 = CP/M .COM build
0000                CHECKED:   EQU   0   ; 1 = checked build
0000                EDITOR:   EQU   1   ; 1 = with the line editor
0000                EDGEN:    EQU   EDITOR*(1-CPM)   ; (the generic build with the editor)
0000                             ; (IF takes any value but 0 as true, so
0000                             ;  IF CHECKED+EDITOR means "either")
0000                TABP0:    EQU   EDGEN*(1-CHECKED)   ; (the build with its table in page zero)
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Register use, everywhere in the interpreter
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    BC   IP: the address of the next program character to read
0000                             ;    HL   TOS: the top data-stack cell is kept here, not in memory
0000                             ;    SP   the data stack: (SP) is NOS, the cell under TOS. The data stack is
0000                             ;         the Z80"s own stack, which is what the spec"s machine-code contract
0000                             ;         needs ("the data cells above the return address").
0000                             ;    HL'  return-stack pointer (the alternate HL). Entries are 2 bytes; the
0000                             ;         stack grows down. Only rpop and rpushn (and the checks) touch it.
0000                             ;    A DE scratch. Every handler is entered with HL = TOS and may use A, DE.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  One-byte calls. The routines used most are reached with RST, one byte
0000                             ;  instead of three:
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    RST 08h  rpop    pop the return stack into DE
0000                             ;    RST 18h  drop    drop TOS, then next character     (ends a handler)
0000                             ;    RST 20h  neg16   HL = -HL
0000                             ;    RST 28h  putc    print A
0000                             ;    RST 30h  next    next character                    (ends a handler)
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  RST 18h and RST 30h never return: an RST is a CALL, so the first thing
0000                             ;  each of them does is POP DE to throw the return address away.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The CP/M build can't own page zero, so the block from `vecs` to `vecend`
0000                             ;  (image addresses 0108h-0133h) is copied to 0008h-0033h when it starts. The
0000                             ;  code in that block is written to work at either place.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Dispatch. PTAB holds one byte per punctuation character: the low byte of
0000                             ;  its handler's address. The high byte is worked out from the character:
0000                             ;  the handlers of the first NPG1 characters (in code order) start in the
0000                             ;  image's second page, the rest in its first. The layout below keeps to
0000                             ;  that, and testing/chktab.py checks it in every build.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Memory map. Everything the interpreter writes is in four RAM pages:
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    RSPAGE   return stack, 112 entries (the pointer stays inside this page)
0000                             ;    DSPAGE   data stack, 127 cells (the top four bytes of the page are spare,
0000                             ;             so a full stack runs two bytes into the page below)
0000                             ;    LETPAGE  letter cells: A..Z at +00h..+33h, a..z at +40h..+73h (so a word
0000                             ;             cell is always 64 bytes below its variable), the heap pointer at
0000                             ;             +7Ch, interpreter variables in the gaps, and the -n? line buffer
0000                             ;             at +80h..+FFh
0000                             ;    PROG     the program text, NUL-terminated; the heap starts after the NUL
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The stacks sit below the letter page, so "the program's own space" (what
0000                             ;  the checked build lets ! and . write) is the single range from the letter
0000                             ;  page up to the heap limit. Each stack has a guard band: the data stack can
0000                             ;  overrun by a cell or two (and the calls made while it is full, the error
0000                             ;  report's included) into the top 32 bytes of the return-stack page, which
0000                             ;  are never used, and the return stack by one entry into the page below it.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                          IF   CPM   
                    BDOS:     EQU   0005h   
                    BASE:     EQU   0100h   ; where the image starts
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   CPM*(1-EDITOR)   
                    EXIT:     EQU   0000h   ; warm boot
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IFN   CPM   
0000                             ; ---- generic machine: edit these to suit -----------------------------------
0000                KEY:      EQU   0FF06h   ; a waiting key in A, or A = 0 if none is
0000                             ;   waiting. The zero flag must match A
0000                             ;   (end the routine with OR A / RET).
0000                CONOUT:   EQU   0FF03h   ; print the character in A
0000                             ;   KEY and CONOUT must preserve BC, DE, HL and HL'.
0000                RSPAGE:   EQU   80h   ; 8000h return stack
0000                DSPAGE:   EQU   81h   ; 8100h data stack
0000                LETPAGE:   EQU   82h   ; 8200h letter cells and line buffer
0000                PROG:     EQU   8300h   ; where the loader puts the program text
0000                HEAPLIM:   EQU   0F0h   ; the heap must stay below F000h (a page)
0000                BASE:     EQU   0000h   ; where the image starts
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)   
                    EXIT:     EQU   0FF09h   ; where to go when the program ends
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   EDGEN   
0000                LEAVE:    EQU   0FF09h   ; where the editor's ^X goes
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   EDITOR*CPM   
                    LEAVE:    EQU   0000h   ; the editor's ^X: warm boot
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   EDITOR   
0000                EXIT:     EQU   edend   ; a program that ends goes back to the editor,
0000                SKEND:    EQU   skend   ;   also when it ends inside skip
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   1-EDITOR   
                    SKEND:    EQU   EXIT   
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                MSLOOP:   EQU   40   ; n? inner loop count for about 1 ms (1-255):
0000                             ; each pass calls getk once, so tune it for
0000                             ; your clock and your KEY routine. (The wait
0000                             ; for a second Ctrl-C uses it too: 250 ms.)
0000                             ; letter-page layout (offsets inside LETPAGE)
0000                LET:      EQU   LETPAGE*256   
0000                HEAP:     EQU   LET+7Ch   ; the heap pointer
0000                RSAVE:    EQU   LET+34h   ; gap after Z: return stack pointer, saved
0000                             ;   around machine code;
0000                NPEND:    EQU   LET+38h   ;   minus the address of the program's end
0000                             ;   (the heap"s first byte), for the checked "_';
0000                EDLN:     EQU   LET+3Ah   ;   the editor: the number of the line that ^E
0000                             ;   put in the input line (0: none)
0000                KEYBUF:   EQU   LET+7Ah   ; gap after z: a key read by the break check and
0000                             ;   held for the next "?" (0: none);
0000                BRKOFF:   EQU   LET+7Bh   ;   the break-off cell: a program that stores a
0000                             ;   non-zero byte here gets Ctrl-C as a key
0000                LBHDR:    EQU   LET+7Eh   ; CP/M BDOS 10 header: max, count
0000                LINEBUF:   EQU   LET+80h   ; -n? text, ending in CR
0000                RSTOP:    EQU   RSPAGE*256+0E0h   ; empty return stack: the 32 bytes above it
0000                             ; take calls made while the data stack is full
0000                DSTOP:    EQU   DSPAGE*256+0FCh   ; empty data stack. The four bytes above it
0000                             ; are spare: a character can pop two cells
0000                             ; too many before the checked build sees it,
0000                             ; and the next call must not land on the
0000                             ; letter cells.
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                             ;  The first 49 bytes: the entry, then the RST routines, with small handlers
0000                             ;  and routines filling the gaps between them. Generic: this IS page zero.
0000                             ;  CP/M: it is the start of the .COM file, and 0108h-0133h is also copied to
0000                             ;  page zero (see the header).
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                          .ORG   BASE   
0000                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)*CHECKED   
                              XOR   A   ; 00  reset. (This byte, AFh, is also what an
0000                          ENDIF      ;     undefined word runs into: see e_hi.)
0000                          IF   1-EDGEN   
                              LD   SP,DSTOP   ; 00  reset, or the start of the .COM file
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)*(1-CHECKED)   
                              LD   BC,PROG   ; 03  the IP
                              JR   st0   ; 06  (the rest of the startup is close by)
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)*CHECKED   
                              JR   init   ; 04  (the rest of the startup is close by)
                              DW   0   ; 06  spare
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   EDGEN   
0000   AF                     XOR   A   ; 00  reset: no program yet. (This byte, AFh,
0001   32 00 83               LD   (PROG),A   ;     is also what an undefined word runs
0004   C3 57 03               JP   init   ; 04  into in the checked build: see e_hi.)
0007   00                     NOP      ; 07  spare
0008                          ENDIF      
0008                          IF   CPM   
                              JP   start   ; 03
                              DW   0   ; 06  spare
0008                          ENDIF      
0008                VECS:        
0008                             ; ---- RST 08h: rpop: pop the return stack into DE ---------------------------
0008   D9           RPOP:     EXX      ; 08
0009   5E                     LD   E,(HL)   
000A   23                     INC   HL   
000B   56                     LD   D,(HL)   
000C   23                     INC   HL   
000D   D5                     PUSH   DE   ; across to the main registers
000E   D9                     EXX      
000F   D1                     POP   DE   
0010   C9                     RET      ; 10  (so RST 10h is not used)
0011                             ; ctl: the inner loop comes here for characters below 21h. A = c - 21h.
0011   C6 21        CTL:      ADD   A,21h   ; 11  back to c; zero only for NUL
0013   20 1C                  JR   NZ,next0   ;     the rest are ignored
0015   C3 97 03     ENDPROG:   JP   EXIT   ;     the program has ended
0018                             ; ---- RST 18h: drop TOS, then next ------------------------------------------
0018   D1           RST18:    POP   DE   ; 18  discard the RST's return address
0019   E1                     POP   HL   ;     new TOS = NOS
001A   18 15                  JR   nx   
001C   E5           H_FROMR:   PUSH   HL   ; 1C  "}" return stack to TOS
001D   CF                     RST   08h   
001E   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
001F   F7                     RST   30h   
0020                             ; ---- RST 20h: neg16: HL = -HL (keeps BC, DE) -------------------------------
0020   AF           NEG16:    XOR   A   ; 20
0021   95                     SUB   L   
0022   6F                     LD   L,A   
0023   9F                     SBC   A,A   
0024   94                     SUB   H   
0025   67                     LD   H,A   
0026   C9                     RET      
0027   00                     NOP      ; 27  spare
0028                             ; ---- RST 28h: putc: print A (keeps BC, DE, HL, HL') ------------------------
0028                RST28:       
0028                          IFN   CPM   
0028   C3 03 FF     PUTC:     JP   CONOUT   ; 28
002B                          ENDIF      
002B                          IF   CPM   
                              JP   putc   ; 28
002B                          ENDIF      
002B   E9           JPHL:     JP   (HL)   ; 2B  (for the machine-code call)
002C   E3           H_TOR:    EX   (SP),HL   ; 2C  "{" TOS to the return stack: the new TOS
002D   C3 CC 00               JP   rpushn   ;     comes up, the old one goes across
0030                             ; ---- RST 30h: next character -----------------------------------------------
0030   D1           RST30:    POP   DE   ; 30  discard the RST's return address
0031                NX:          
0031                          IF   CPM   
                              JP   next0   ; (this copy runs in page zero)
0031                          ENDIF      
0031                VECEND:      
0031                             ; =============================================================================
0031                             ;  The inner loop: read one character and sort it by range.
0031                             ; 
0031                             ;    00h          end of program
0031                             ;    01h-20h, 7Fh-FFh   ignored (control, space, DEL, high bytes)
0031                             ;    30h-39h      digit: read a whole number
0031                             ;    41h-5Ah      A-Z: call the word in that letter's cell
0031                             ;    61h-7Ah      a-z: push the address of that letter's cell
0031                             ;    the rest     punctuation: jump through PTAB, 32 entries, in code order
0031                             ; =============================================================================
0031                NEXT0:       
0031                          IF   CHECKED   
                              CALL   chkstk   ; both stacks are checked once per character
0031                          ENDIF      
0031   0A                     LD   A,(BC)   
0032   03                     INC   BC   
0033   D6 21                  SUB   21h   ; A = c - 21h
0035   38 DA                  JR   C,ctl   ; c < 21h: NUL ends, the rest are ignored
0037   FE 0F                  CP   0Fh   
0039   38 22                  JR   C,punct   ; 21h-2Fh: PTAB index 0-14
003B   D6 0F                  SUB   0Fh   ; A = c - 30h
003D   FE 0A                  CP   0Ah   
003F   38 75                  JR   C,digit   ; 30h-39h
0041   FE 11                  CP   11h   
0043   38 16                  JR   C,p3a   ; 3Ah-40h
0045   D6 11                  SUB   11h   ; A = c - 41h
0047   FE 1A                  CP   1Ah   
0049   38 77                  JR   C,upper   ; 41h-5Ah: A = letter index 0-25
004B   FE 20                  CP   20h   
004D   38 0A                  JR   C,p5b   ; 5Bh-60h
004F   FE 3A                  CP   3Ah   
0051   38 69                  JR   C,lower   ; 61h-7Ah: A = 20h-39h (cell +64 bytes)
0053   FE 3E                  CP   3Eh   
0055                          IF   1-CHECKED   
0055   30 DA                  JR   NC,next0   ; 7Fh-FFh: ignored
0057                          ENDIF      
0057                          IF   CHECKED   
                              JR   Z,next0   ; 7Fh, DEL: ignored
                              JP   NC,e_hi   ; 80h-FFh: reserved
0057                          ENDIF      
0057   D6 1A                  SUB   1Ah   ; 7Bh-7Eh: -1Eh in all, index 28-31
0059   D6 09        P5B:      SUB   9   ; 5Bh-60h: -4 in all, index 22-27
005B   C6 05        P3A:      ADD   A,5   ; 3Ah-40h: index 15-21
005D                .macro PTABLE,
005D                             ; 
005D                 DB      h_store & 0FFh  ; !
005D                 DB      h_str & 0FFh    ; "
005D                 DB      h_num & 0FFh    ; #
005D                 DB      h_print & 0FFh  ; $
005D                 DB      h_swap & 0FFh   ; %
005D                 DB      h_and & 0FFh    ; &
005D                 DB      h_emit & 0FFh   ; '
005D                 DB      h_open & 0FFh   ; (
005D                 DB      h_close & 0FFh  ; )
005D                 DB      h_mul & 0FFh    ; *
005D                 DB      h_add & 0FFh    ; +
005D                 DB      h_cfetch & 0FFh ; ,
005D                 DB      h_sub & 0FFh    ; -
005D                 DB      h_cstore & 0FFh ; .
005D                 DB      h_div & 0FFh    ; /
005D                 DB      h_dup & 0FFh    ; :
005D                 DB      h_drop & 0FFh   ; ;
005D                 DB      h_lt & 0FFh     ; <
005D                 DB      h_eq & 0FFh     ; =
005D                 DB      h_gt & 0FFh     ; >
005D                 DB      h_key & 0FFh    ; ?
005D                 DB      h_fetch & 0FFh  ; @
005D                 DB      h_def & 0FFh    ; [
005D                 DB      h_break & 0FFh  ; \
005D                 DB      h_ret & 0FFh    ; ]
005D                 DB      h_xor & 0FFh    ; ^
005D                 DB      h_alloc & 0FFh  ; _
005D                 DB      h_grave & 0FFh  ; `
005D                 DB      h_tor & 0FFh    ; {
005D                 DB      h_or & 0FFh     ; |
005D                 DB      h_fromr & 0FFh  ; }
005D                 DB      h_not & 0FFh    ; ~
005D                .endm
005D                 
005D                             ; Punctuation: A = the PTAB index. The handler starts with HL = TOS,
005D                             ; untouched, and A, DE free.
005D   C6 6A        PUNCT:    ADD   A,PTAB & 0FFh   ; PTAB never crosses a page
005F   5F                     LD   E,A   
0060   16 00                  LD   D,PTAB / 256   ; (0 if the table is in page zero)
0062   FE 81                  CP   (PTAB & 0FFh) + NPG1   ; carry: one of the first NPG1
0064   1A                     LD   A,(DE)   
0065   5F                     LD   E,A   ; the handler's low byte
0066                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-TABP0)   
                              LD   D,0   
0066                          ENDIF      
0066                          IFN   CPM   
0066   CB 12                  RL   D   ; its page: 0 + carry
0068                          ENDIF      
0068                          IF   CPM   
                              LD   D,1   
                              JR   NC,pu1   
                              INC   D   ; its page: 1 + carry
                    PU1:         
0068                          ENDIF      
0068   D5                     PUSH   DE   ; jump to it; the stack is balanced again
0069   C9                     RET      ;   when the handler starts
006A                             ; The rest of the startup: here so that the generic reset code can reach it
006A                             ; with JR. st0: find the program's NUL; the heap starts after it.
006A                             ; (The editor build has its own copy of this, next to the editor.)
006A                             ; A checked build first clears the lower half of the letter page (A = 0):
006A                             ; every variable starts at 0, every word cell holds 0000h, the address an
006A                             ; undefined word is caught at (see e_hi), and no key is held back.
006A                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)*CHECKED   
                    INIT:     LD   HL,LET   
                    INI1:     LD   (HL),A   
                              INC   L   
                              JP   P,ini1   ; +00h to +7Fh
                              LD   BC,PROG   ; the IP
006A                          ENDIF      
006A                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)   
                    ST0:      LD   H,B   
                              LD   L,C   
                              XOR   A   
                    ST1:      CP   (HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              JR   NZ,st1   
006A                          ENDIF      
006A                          IF   1-EDITOR   
                    ST2:      LD   (HEAP),HL   
006A                          ENDIF      
006A                          IF   CHECKED*(1-EDITOR)   
                              RST   20h   ; minus the heap"s first address: "_' may not
                              LD   (NPEND),HL   ;   release below it
006A                          ENDIF      
006A                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*(1-EDITOR)   
                              LD   HL,0   ; no key is held, and the break key is on
                              LD   (KEYBUF),HL   ;   (the checked build has cleared these)
006A                          ENDIF      
006A                          IF   1-EDITOR   
                              EXX      
                              LD   HL,RSTOP   ; the return stack is empty
                              EXX      
                              RST   30h   ; (its return address is thrown away)
006A                          ENDIF      
006A                             ; In the unchecked generic editor build the table is here, in the first
006A                             ; page, which saves loading D twice. (The other builds have no room for it
006A                             ; here: theirs is further down.)
006A                          IF   TABP0   
006A                PTAB:        
006A                          ;*Macro unroll:  PTABLE
006A   A5                     DB   h_store & 0FFh   
006B   AA                     DB   h_str & 0FFh   
006C   B8                     DB   h_num & 0FFh   
006D   B1                     DB   h_print & 0FFh   
006E   A0                     DB   h_swap & 0FFh   
006F   48                     DB   h_and & 0FFh   
0070   B5                     DB   h_emit & 0FFh   
0071   24                     DB   h_open & 0FFh   
0072   2C                     DB   h_close & 0FFh   
0073   69                     DB   h_mul & 0FFh   
0074   3F                     DB   h_add & 0FFh   
0075   D6                     DB   h_cfetch & 0FFh   
0076   37                     DB   h_sub & 0FFh   
0077   A2                     DB   h_cstore & 0FFh   
0078   7D                     DB   h_div & 0FFh   
0079   9E                     DB   h_dup & 0FFh   
007A   A4                     DB   h_drop & 0FFh   
007B   50                     DB   h_lt & 0FFh   
007C   5F                     DB   h_eq & 0FFh   
007D   51                     DB   h_gt & 0FFh   
007E   BE                     DB   h_key & 0FFh   
007F   1F                     DB   h_fetch & 0FFh   
0080   02                     DB   h_def & 0FFh   
0081   F5                     DB   h_break & 0FFh   
0082   F1                     DB   h_ret & 0FFh   
0083   8A                     DB   h_xor & 0FFh   
0084   9D                     DB   h_alloc & 0FFh   
0085   DB                     DB   h_grave & 0FFh   
0086   2C                     DB   h_tor & 0FFh   
0087   92                     DB   h_or & 0FFh   
0088   1C                     DB   h_fromr & 0FFh   
0089   9A                     DB   h_not & 0FFh   
008A                PTABEND:      
008A                          ENDIF      
008A                             ; =============================================================================
008A                             ;  Handlers that must start in the image's first page: ^ _ ` | ~
008A                             ;  (00bbIGFuZCA= are up among the RST routines.) The machine-code call, exec,
008A                             ;  is here too: it belongs to "`" and makes the page come out right.
008A                             ; =============================================================================
008A   D1           H_XOR:    POP   DE   
008B   7C                     LD   A,H   
008C   AA                     XOR   D   
008D   67                     LD   H,A   
008E   7D                     LD   A,L   
008F   AB                     XOR   E   
0090   6F                     LD   L,A   
0091   F7                     RST   30h   
0092   D1           H_OR:     POP   DE   
0093   7C                     LD   A,H   
0094   B2                     OR   D   
0095   67                     LD   H,A   
0096   7D                     LD   A,L   
0097   B3                     OR   E   
0098   6F                     LD   L,A   
0099   F7                     RST   30h   
009A   E7           H_NOT:    RST   20h   ; ~x = -x - 1
009B   2B                     DEC   HL   
009C   F7                     RST   30h   
009D                             ; "_" ( n -- addr ): the heap pointer moves by n, a signed count (the add is
009D                             ; the same either way); TOS is the old pointer.
009D   ED 5B 7C 82  H_ALLOC:   LD   DE,(HEAP)   
00A1                          IF   CHECKED*CPM   
                              LD   A,H   ; the count's sign, for chkhp
00A1                          ENDIF      
00A1   19                     ADD   HL,DE   ; the new top
00A2                          IF   CHECKED   
                              CALL   chkhp   
00A2                          ENDIF      
00A2   22 7C 82               LD   (HEAP),HL   
00A5   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
00A6   F7                     RST   30h   
00A7   D9           EXEC:     EXX      
00A8   22 34 82               LD   (RSAVE),HL   ; machine code may change the alternates
00AB   D9                     EXX      
00AC   CD 2B 00               CALL   jphl   
00AF   D9                     EXX      
00B0   2A 34 82               LD   HL,(RSAVE)   
00B3   D9                     EXX      
00B4   E1                     POP   HL   
00B5   F7                     RST   30h   
00B6                             ; ---- the letters and digits (here, in the middle, so that the inner loop's
00B6                             ; ---- short jumps reach them, and the handlers after them reach rpushn) ------
00B6                             ; Digits: step back onto the first digit and read the whole number.
00B6   E5           DIGIT:    PUSH   HL   
00B7   0B                     DEC   BC   
00B8   CD 2F 02               CALL   rdnum   
00BB   F7                     RST   30h   
00BC                             ; a-z: push the cell's address (the cell is the variable)
00BC   E5           LOWER:    PUSH   HL   
00BD   87                     ADD   A,A   
00BE   6F                     LD   L,A   
00BF   26 82                  LD   H,LETPAGE   
00C1   F7                     RST   30h   
00C2                             ; A-Z: call the word. The return address (the IP after the letter) goes on
00C2                             ; the return stack, and the IP becomes the address in the letter's cell.
00C2   C5           UPPER:    PUSH   BC   ; the return address, for rpushn
00C3   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; park TOS
00C4   87                     ADD   A,A   
00C5   6F                     LD   L,A   
00C6   26 82                  LD   H,LETPAGE   ; HL -> cell
00C8   4E                     LD   C,(HL)   
00C9   2C                     INC   L   
00CA   46                     LD   B,(HL)   ; IP = the word's body
00CB   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; TOS back, and fall into rpushn
00CC                             ; rpushn: move the top cell of the data stack (in memory) to the return
00CC                             ; stack, then next. Everything that pushes the return stack ends here.
00CC                             ; 
00CC                             ; The break key is looked at here, so at every word call and loop-back (and
00CC                             ; block entry and "{"), but only one time in 256: B', which nothing else
00CC                             ; uses, counts them. Reading the keyboard can be slow (it is a BDOS call
00CC                             ; under CP/M), and this way it costs a loop two bytes and 13 T-states.
00CC   D9           RPUSHN:   EXX      
00CD   D1                     POP   DE   
00CE   2B                     DEC   HL   
00CF   72                     LD   (HL),D   
00D0   2B                     DEC   HL   
00D1   73                     LD   (HL),E   
00D2   10 05                  DJNZ   rp1   
00D4   D9                     EXX      
00D5   CD 9E 02               CALL   pollk   
00D8   F7                     RST   30h   
00D9   D9           RP1:      EXX      
00DA   F7                     RST   30h   
00DB                             ; ---- machine code: the grave -----------------------------------------------
00DB                             ; "`" plus a hex digit loads bytes: ( addr -- addr' ). Pairs of hex digits
00DB                             ; are stored from addr until a non-hex character; then a RET (C9h) is
00DB                             ; written and its address is left. An odd last digit is consumed and dropped.
00DB                             ; "`" plus anything else calls the machine code at TOS: ( addr -- ). The
00DB                             ; code is entered by CALL with the data stack above the return address; it
00DB                             ; must keep BC, and on return the top cell becomes the new TOS.
00DB   CD 8C 02     H_GRAVE:   CALL   hexc   
00DE   30 C7                  JR   NC,exec   
00E0   77           HX1:      LD   (HL),A   ; the high digit goes in first ...
00E1   CD 8C 02               CALL   hexc   
00E4   30 08                  JR   NC,hx2   ; odd digit: consumed, and the RET below
00E6   ED 6F                  RLD      ;   overwrites it
00E8   23                     INC   HL   ; ... and RLD shifts it up under the low one
00E9   CD 8C 02               CALL   hexc   
00EC   38 F2                  JR   C,hx1   
00EE   36 C9        HX2:      LD   (HL),0C9h   ; (never range-checked: the spec says so)
00F0   F7                     RST   30h   
00F1                             ; ---- where the two pages meet ----------------------------------------------
00F1                             ; The first page ends somewhere among the next four handlers, ] \ [ @ (they
00F1                             ; are in falling code order for this), and where exactly differs between the
00F1                             ; builds: NPG1 follows. Every handler below these four must start in the
00F1                             ; second page, and every one above in the first; chktab.py checks both.
00F1                             ; "]" returns: pop an address and jump to it.
00F1   CF           H_RET:    RST   08h   
00F2   42                     LD   B,D   
00F3   4B                     LD   C,E   
00F4   F7           BRK1:     RST   30h   
00F5                             ; "\" ( flag -- ): true skips to the next ")" or "]" at this level; ")"
00F5                             ; drops the block start, "]" returns. No closer at all ends the program.
00F5   7C           H_BREAK:   LD   A,H   
00F6   B5                     OR   L   
00F7   E1                     POP   HL   
00F8   28 FA                  JR   Z,brk1   
00FA   CD 51 02               CALL   skip   
00FD   B7                     OR   A   ; skip returns 0 for ")"
00FE   20 F1                  JR   NZ,h_ret   
0100   CF           RDROP:    RST   08h   
0101   F7                     RST   30h   
0102                             ; "[" followed by a letter stores the body"s address in that letter"s cell:
0102                             ; uppercase is a word, lowercase a variable. Followed by a space it pushes
0102                             ; the body"s address instead. Either way it then skips to the matching "]'.
0102                             ; (The unchecked build takes anything that is not a letter as the space; the
0102                             ; checked build stops on it.)
0102   0A           H_DEF:    LD   A,(BC)   
0103   03                     INC   BC   
0104   D6 41                  SUB   "A"   ; a letter gives 0-25 or 32-57: lowercase
0106   5F                     LD   E,A   ;   lands 64 bytes up
0107   E6 DF                  AND   0DFh   ; fold case
0109   FE 1A                  CP   26   
010B   30 0B                  JR   NC,def2   ; not a letter
010D   CB 23                  SLA   E   
010F   16 82                  LD   D,LETPAGE   ; DE -> cell
0111   79                     LD   A,C   
0112   12                     LD   (DE),A   
0113   1C                     INC   E   
0114   78                     LD   A,B   
0115   12                     LD   (DE),A   
0116   18 03                  JR   skipnx   
0118                DEF2:        
0118                          IF   CHECKED   
                              LD   A,E   
                              CP   " "-"A"+256   
                              JP   NZ,e_brack   ; anything but a letter or a space
0118                          ENDIF      
0118   E5                     PUSH   HL   ; an anonymous block: push its address
0119   60                     LD   H,B   
011A   69                     LD   L,C   
011B                SKIPNX:      
011B                          IF   CHECKED   
                              DEC   BC   ; back onto the letter, so that skip finds its
011B                          ENDIF      ;   opener, the "[", just before where it starts
011B   CD 51 02     SKIPO:    CALL   skip   
011E   F7                     RST   30h   
011F   5E           H_FETCH:   LD   E,(HL)   ; "@"
0120   23                     INC   HL   
0121   56                     LD   D,(HL)   
0122   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
0123   F7                     RST   30h   
0124                             ; =============================================================================
0124                             ;  Handlers that must start in the image's second page.
0124                             ;  "?" is the last (with "," inside it), so its long tail may run past that
0124                             ;  page.
0124                             ; =============================================================================
0124                             ; "(" ( flag -- ): true pushes the block start and enters; false skips to
0124                             ; the matching ")".
0124   7C           H_OPEN:   LD   A,H   
0125   B5                     OR   L   
0126   E1                     POP   HL   
0127   28 F2                  JR   Z,skipo   
0129   C5                     PUSH   BC   ; the block starts at the IP
012A   18 A0                  JR   rpushn   
012C                             ; ")" ( flag -- ): true jumps back to the block start (and keeps it); false
012C                             ; drops it and carries on.
012C   7C           H_CLOSE:   LD   A,H   
012D   B5                     OR   L   
012E   E1                     POP   HL   
012F   28 CF                  JR   Z,rdrop   
0131   CF                     RST   08h   ; pop the block start ...
0132   42                     LD   B,D   
0133   4B                     LD   C,E   
0134   C5                     PUSH   BC   
0135   18 95                  JR   rpushn   ; ... and push it back
0137                             ; ---- arithmetic and logic: ( NOS TOS -- result ) ---------------------------
0137                             ; "-" has two jobs: directly before a digit it starts a negative number.
0137   0A           H_SUB:    LD   A,(BC)   
0138   D6 30                  SUB   "0"   
013A   FE 0A                  CP   10   
013C   38 04                  JR   C,negnum   
013E   E7                     RST   20h   ; a - b = a + (-b): fall into "+"
013F   D1           H_ADD:    POP   DE   
0140   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
0141   F7                     RST   30h   
0142   E5           NEGNUM:   PUSH   HL   ; a negative number: read it, negate it
0143   CD 2F 02               CALL   rdnum   
0146   E7                     RST   20h   
0147   F7                     RST   30h   
0148   D1           H_AND:    POP   DE   
0149   7C                     LD   A,H   
014A   A2                     AND   D   
014B   67                     LD   H,A   
014C   7D                     LD   A,L   
014D   A3                     AND   E   
014E   6F                     LD   L,A   
014F   F7                     RST   30h   
0150                             ; Signed compares. Both are "HL < DE" for the right pair: "<" swaps the two
0150                             ; cells first. Flipping both sign bits turns a signed compare into an
0150                             ; unsigned one (and XOR clears the carry for SBC); SBC HL,HL then turns the
0150                             ; carry into -1 or 0 with no branch.
0150   E3           H_LT:     EX   (SP),HL   ; a < b: HL = a, and b is popped next
0151   D1           H_GT:     POP   DE   ; a > b  is  b < a: HL = b, DE = a
0152   7C                     LD   A,H   
0153   EE 80                  XOR   80h   
0155   67                     LD   H,A   
0156   7A                     LD   A,D   
0157   EE 80                  XOR   80h   
0159   57                     LD   D,A   
015A   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   ; carry if HL < DE
015C   ED 62        TF:       SBC   HL,HL   ; carry -> -1 or 0
015E   F7                     RST   30h   
015F   D1           H_EQ:     POP   DE   
0160   B7                     OR   A   
0161   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   
0163   7C                     LD   A,H   
0164   B5                     OR   L   
0165   FE 01                  CP   1   ; carry only if a - b = 0
0167   18 F3                  JR   tf   
0169                             ; "*": shift-and-add, 16 rounds; only the low 16 bits are kept. The
0169                             ; multiplier shifts up through A:C.
0169   D1           H_MUL:    POP   DE   ; DE = multiplicand
016A   C5                     PUSH   BC   
016B   7C                     LD   A,H   
016C   4D                     LD   C,L   ; A:C = multiplier
016D   21 00 00               LD   HL,0   
0170   06 10                  LD   B,16   
0172   29           MUL1:     ADD   HL,HL   
0173   CB 21                  SLA   C   
0175   17                     RLA      
0176   30 01                  JR   NC,mul2   
0178   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
0179   10 F7        MUL2:     DJNZ   mul1   
017B   C1                     POP   BC   
017C   F7                     RST   30h   
017D                             ; "/" ( a b -- q r ): the remainder is on top. Truncates toward zero; r takes
017D                             ; a's sign. Divide |a| by |b|, then q gets the sign of a XOR b and r the sign
017D                             ; of a. Dividing by zero returns two cells of no meaning; the checked build
017D                             ; stops on it.
017D                H_DIV:       
017D                          IF   CHECKED   
                              LD   A,H   
                              OR   L   
                              JP   Z,e_zero   
017D                          ENDIF      
017D   D1                     POP   DE   ; DE = a, HL = b
017E   C5                     PUSH   BC   ; free BC for udiv
017F   D5                     PUSH   DE   ; a, for r's sign
0180   7A                     LD   A,D   
0181   AC                     XOR   H   
0182   F5                     PUSH   AF   ; S flag = sign of q
0183   CB 7C                  BIT   7,H   
0185   C4 20 00               CALL   NZ,neg16   ; HL = |b|
0188   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
0189   CB 7C                  BIT   7,H   
018B   C4 20 00               CALL   NZ,neg16   ; HL = |a|, DE = |b|
018E   CD 09 02               CALL   udiv   ; HL = q, DE = r
0191   F1                     POP   AF   
0192   FC 20 00               CALL   M,neg16   ; q's sign
0195   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; HL = r, DE = q
0196   F1                     POP   AF   ; A = a's high byte
0197   B7                     OR   A   
0198   FC 20 00               CALL   M,neg16   ; r's sign
019B   C1                     POP   BC   
019C   D5                     PUSH   DE   ; q under r
019D   F7                     RST   30h   
019E                             ; ---- stack and storage -----------------------------------------------------
019E   E5           H_DUP:    PUSH   HL   ; ":"
019F   F7                     RST   30h   
01A0   E3           H_SWAP:   EX   (SP),HL   ; "%"
01A1   F7                     RST   30h   
01A2                             ; (The checked build tests the address before it takes the value off the
01A2                             ; stack, so that an error report shows both.)
01A2                H_CSTORE:      ; "." ( c addr -- )
01A2                          IF   CHECKED   
                              CALL   chkst   
01A2                          ENDIF      
01A2   D1                     POP   DE   
01A3   73                     LD   (HL),E   
01A4   DF           H_DROP:   RST   18h   ; ";" is this one byte
01A5                H_STORE:      ; "!" ( n addr -- )
01A5                          IF   CHECKED   
                              CALL   chkst   
01A5                          ENDIF      
01A5   D1                     POP   DE   
01A6   73                     LD   (HL),E   
01A7   23                     INC   HL   
01A8   72                     LD   (HL),D   
01A9   DF                     RST   18h   
01AA                             ; ---- console ---------------------------------------------------------------
01AA                             ; 22h pushes the address of the text after it and skips the string.
01AA   E5           H_STR:    PUSH   HL   
01AB   60                     LD   H,B   
01AC   69                     LD   L,C   
01AD   CD 46 02               CALL   skipstr   
01B0                          IF   CHECKED   
                              OR   A   ; 0: the text ran out before the closing quote
                              JP   Z,e_quote   
01B0                          ENDIF      
01B0   F7                     RST   30h   
01B1                             ; "$" prints the string at TOS, decoding escapes: "/" plus a character
01B1                             ; clears that character"s bit 6 (/M is CR, /` is space; "/" and ""' have no
01B1                             ; bit 6, so // and /" give themselves).
01B1                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*(1-EDITOR)   
                    H_PRINT:   LD   A,(HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              CP   22h   
                              JR   Z,pr9   
                              CP   "/"   
                              JR   NZ,pr1   
                              LD   A,(HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              AND   0BFh   
                    PR1:      RST   28h   
                              JR   h_print   
01B1                          ENDIF      
01B1                          IF   CHECKED   
                                 ; (The checked build has the loop as a routine, prstr, which the error
                                 ; report uses too. The address is kept on the stack meanwhile: a report
                                 ; shows the stack as it was before the "$".)
                    H_PRINT:   PUSH   HL   
                              CALL   prstr   
                              POP   DE   
                              RST   18h   
01B1                          ENDIF      
01B1                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*EDITOR   
01B1                             ; (With the editor the loop is a routine, prstr, which ^V uses too.)
01B1   CD 3B 03     H_PRINT:   CALL   prstr   
01B4   DF                     RST   18h   
01B5                          ENDIF      
01B5   7D           H_EMIT:   LD   A,L   ; "'"
01B6   EF                     RST   28h   
01B7   DF           PR9:      RST   18h   
01B8                             ; "#" prints TOS as a signed decimal number, with no space after it.
01B8   C5           H_NUM:    PUSH   BC   
01B9   CD 72 02               CALL   psgn   
01BC   C1                     POP   BC   
01BD   DF                     RST   18h   
01BE                             ; "?" ( n -- c ) or ( -n -- addr )
01BE                             ;   n > 0: wait about n ms for a key; 0 if none came
01BE                             ;   n = 0: wait for a key
01BE                             ;   n < 0: read a line of at most -n characters, with echo. The buffer
01BE                             ;          holds 127 characters and the CR: a bigger count is taken as 127.
01BE   CB 7C        H_KEY:    BIT   7,H   
01C0   20 19                  JR   NZ,line   
01C2   1E 28        KT1:      LD   E,MSLOOP   ; one millisecond, roughly
01C4   CD AA 02     KT2:      CALL   getk   
01C7   20 0E                  JR   NZ,kt3   
01C9   1D                     DEC   E   
01CA   20 F8                  JR   NZ,kt2   
01CC   7C                     LD   A,H   ; 0? never counts down: it waits
01CD   B5                     OR   L   
01CE   28 F2                  JR   Z,kt1   
01D0   2B                     DEC   HL   
01D1   7C                     LD   A,H   
01D2   B5                     OR   L   
01D3   20 ED                  JR   NZ,kt1   ; A = 0 if the time ran out
01D5   FE                     DB   0FEh   ; (CP n: steps over the one byte of ",")
01D6   7E           H_CFETCH:   LD   A,(HL)   ; "," shares "?"s ending: A becomes TOS
01D7   6F           KT3:      LD   L,A   
01D8   26 00                  LD   H,0   
01DA   F7                     RST   30h   
01DB                          IF   CPM   
                                 ; CP/M: BDOS 10 does the editing (the spec allows the platform's
                                 ; own line editor). It doesn't store the CR, so it is added here.
                    LINE:     LD   DE,127   ; TOS is minus the count: adding 127 carries
                              ADD   HL,DE   ;   only for 1 to 127, and leaves 127 - count
                              SBC   A,A   
                              AND   L   ; (0 for a count that is too big)
                              XOR   127   ; A = the count, 127 at most
                              LD   (LBHDR),A   
                              LD   DE,LBHDR   
                              LD   A,10   
                              CALL   bdosx   
                              LD   HL,LBHDR+1   
                              LD   A,(HL)   ; the count typed (0-127)
                              INC   L   ; HL = LINEBUF, whose low byte is 80h:
                              ADD   A,L   ;   adding the count to L can't carry
                              LD   L,A   
                              LD   (HL),13   
01DB                          ENDIF      
01DB                          IFN   CPM   
01DB                             ; Generic: Backspace takes the last character back (and is echoed as
01DB                             ; it is), CR ends (stored, not echoed), every other key is stored and
01DB                             ; echoed until the line is full. The line buffer starts at offset 80h
01DB                             ; of its page, so L alone is the place in the line: D holds the L of
01DB                             ; a full line.
01DB   11 7F 00     LINE:     LD   DE,127   ; TOS is minus the count: adding 127 carries
01DE   19                     ADD   HL,DE   ;   only for 1 to 127, and leaves 127 - count
01DF   9F                     SBC   A,A   
01E0   A5                     AND   L   ; (0 for a count that is too big)
01E1   2F                     CPL      
01E2   57                     LD   D,A   ; D = the L of a full line: 80h + count, FFh
01E3                             ;   at most
01E3   21 80 82               LD   HL,LINEBUF   
01E6   CD AA 02     LN2:      CALL   getk   
01E9   28 FB                  JR   Z,ln2   
01EB   FE 0D                  CP   13   
01ED   28 16                  JR   Z,ln5   
01EF   FE 08                  CP   8   
01F1   28 0B                  JR   Z,ln4   
01F3   5F                     LD   E,A   
01F4   7D                     LD   A,L   
01F5   BA                     CP   D   
01F6   28 EE                  JR   Z,ln2   ; full
01F8   73                     LD   (HL),E   
01F9   2C                     INC   L   
01FA   7B                     LD   A,E   
01FB   EF           LN3:      RST   28h   
01FC   18 E8                  JR   ln2   
01FE   2D           LN4:      DEC   L   ; Backspace: one back, and echo it,
01FF   FA FB 01               JP   M,ln3   ;   unless the line was empty (L left the
0202   2C                     INC   L   ;   upper half of the page)
0203   18 E1                  JR   ln2   
0205   77           LN5:      LD   (HL),A   ; the CR
0206                          ENDIF      
0206   2E 80                  LD   L,LINEBUF & 0FFh   
0208   F7                     RST   30h   
0209                             ; =============================================================================
0209                             ;  More routines (no handler starts past this point)
0209                             ; =============================================================================
0209                             ; udiv: unsigned HL / DE (DE <= 8000h). Returns HL = quotient, DE = remainder.
0209                             ; Uses A, BC; the caller saves the IP. The dividend shifts up through A:C
0209                             ; while the quotient bits arrive at the bottom of C.
0209                             ; Dividing by 2 is one shift (the spec wants that fast).
0209   7B           UDIV:     LD   A,E   
020A   EE 02                  XOR   2   
020C   B2                     OR   D   
020D   20 07                  JR   NZ,udv0   
020F   CB 3C                  SRL   H   
0211   CB 1D                  RR   L   ; the quotient
0213   8F                     ADC   A,A   
0214   5F                     LD   E,A   ; the remainder: the bit that fell out (D is 0)
0215   C9                     RET      
0216   7C           UDV0:     LD   A,H   
0217   4D                     LD   C,L   
0218   21 00 00               LD   HL,0   
021B   06 10                  LD   B,16   
021D   CB 21        UDV1:     SLA   C   
021F   17                     RLA      
0220   ED 6A                  ADC   HL,HL   
0222   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   ; carry is clear here: the remainder
0224   30 02                  JR   NC,udv2   ;   always fits in 16 bits
0226   19                     ADD   HL,DE   ; too much: put it back, and cancel the
0227   0D                     DEC   C   ;   INC below
0228   0C           UDV2:     INC   C   ; a quotient bit
0229   10 F2                  DJNZ   udv1   
022B   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; DE = remainder
022C   67                     LD   H,A   
022D   69                     LD   L,C   ; HL = quotient
022E   C9                     RET      
022F                             ; rdnum: read decimal digits at IP into HL; IP is left on the first
022F                             ; non-digit. Values wrap at 16 bits, as the spec says.
022F   21 00 00     RDNUM:    LD   HL,0   
0232   0A           RDN1:     LD   A,(BC)   
0233   D6 30                  SUB   "0"   
0235   FE 0A                  CP   10   
0237   D0                     RET   NC   
0238   03                     INC   BC   
0239   54                     LD   D,H   
023A   5D                     LD   E,L   
023B   29                     ADD   HL,HL   
023C   29                     ADD   HL,HL   
023D   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
023E   29                     ADD   HL,HL   ; HL * 10
023F   5F                     LD   E,A   
0240   16 00                  LD   D,0   
0242   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
0243   18 ED                  JR   rdn1   
0245                             ; skipstr: IP is inside a string; step past its closing quote. "/" escapes
0245                             ; the next character, so "/"" does not end it. Leaves A = 22h.
0245                          IF   1-CHECKED   
0245   03           SS0:      INC   BC   
0246   0A           SKIPSTR:   LD   A,(BC)   
0247   03                     INC   BC   
0248   FE 2F                  CP   "/"   
024A   28 F9                  JR   Z,ss0   
024C   FE 22                  CP   22h   
024E   20 F6                  JR   NZ,skipstr   
0250   C9                     RET      
0251                          ENDIF      
0251                          IF   CHECKED   
                                 ; The checked build never steps over a NUL: if the text runs out first it
                                 ; returns A = 0 with the IP on the NUL.
                    SKIPSTR:   LD   A,(BC)   
                              OR   A   
                              RET   Z   
                              INC   BC   
                              CP   22h   
                              RET   Z   
                              CP   "/"   
                              JR   NZ,skipstr   
                              LD   A,(BC)   ; the escaped character
                              OR   A   
                              RET   Z   
                              INC   BC   
                              JR   skipstr   
0251                          ENDIF      
0251                             ; skip: read past text to the closer at this level, and return A = 0 if it
0251                             ; was ")" and 2 if it was "]". Brackets of both kinds count together;
0251                             ; strings are stepped over whole. A NUL first ends the program (for "\" with
0251                             ; no closer; anything else that runs into the NUL had unbalanced brackets
0251                             ; anyway). D counts the open levels, starting at 1 for the one we are in:
0251                             ; skip sets it to 0 and falls through the INC that an opener comes back to.
0251                             ; 
0251                             ; The checked build also looks at the character the skip was started by,
0251                             ; which is always the one just before where it starts: "(" must end at ")",
0251                             ; "[" at "]", and neither may run into the NUL (N); a string with no closing
0251                             ; quote counts as running into it. "\" takes either closer. IX keeps the
0251                             ; place where the skip started, for the report.
0251                SKIP:        
0251                          IF   CHECKED   
                              PUSH   BC   
                              POP   IX   
                              DEC   BC   
                              LD   A,(BC)   
                              INC   BC   
                              LD   E,A   ; E = the opener: ( [ or \
0251                          ENDIF      
0251   16 00                  LD   D,0   
0253   14           SK3:      INC   D   ; an opener: one deeper
0254   0A           SK1:      LD   A,(BC)   
0255                          IF   1-CHECKED   
0255   03                     INC   BC   
0256   B7                     OR   A   
0257   CA 96 03               JP   Z,SKEND   ; (the end of the program)
025A                          ENDIF      
025A                          IF   CHECKED   
                              OR   A   
                              JR   Z,sk6   ; (the IP stays on the NUL)
                              INC   BC   
025A                          ENDIF      
025A   FE 22                  CP   22h   
025C   CC 46 02               CALL   Z,skipstr   ; leaves A = 22h, which matches nothing below
025F   D6 28                  SUB   "("   ;   (or 0, and then the NUL is read next)
0261   28 F0                  JR   Z,sk3   
0263   3D                     DEC   A   ; ")"
0264   28 08                  JR   Z,sk4   
0266   D6 32                  SUB   "["-")"   
0268   28 E9                  JR   Z,sk3   
026A   FE 02                  CP   "]"-"["   
026C   20 E6                  JR   NZ,sk1   
026E   15           SK4:      DEC   D   
026F                          IF   1-CHECKED   
026F   C8                     RET   Z   ; the closer at this level
0270   18 E2                  JR   sk1   
0272                          ENDIF      
0272                          IF   CHECKED   
                              JR   NZ,sk1   
                              LD   D,A   ; the closer at this level: 0 or 2. Bit 1 of the
                              XOR   E   ;   opener is 0 for "(" and 1 for "[", and only
                              AND   6   ;   "\" has bit 2: so this is 2 for the wrong
                              CP   2   ;   closer, and only then
                              LD   A,D   
                              RET   NZ   
                              JR   sk7   
                    SK6:      BIT   2,E   ; the text ran out:
                              JP   NZ,SKEND   ;   "\" with no closer ends the program
                    SK7:      PUSH   IX   ; N. The place is the opener
                              POP   BC   
                              LD   A,"N"   
                              JP   errp   ; (errp drops skip's return address)
0272                          ENDIF      
0272                             ; psgn: print HL as a signed number. Uses BC.
0272   CB 7C        PSGN:     BIT   7,H   
0274   28 04                  JR   Z,pdec   
0276   3E 2D                  LD   A,"-"   
0278   EF                     RST   28h   
0279   E7                     RST   20h   
027A                             ; pdec: print HL unsigned, by recursion on HL / 10 (the stack holds digits).
027A                             ; Uses BC.
027A   11 0A 00     PDEC:     LD   DE,10   
027D   CD 09 02               CALL   udiv   ; HL = HL / 10, E = the last digit
0280   7B                     LD   A,E   
0281   F5                     PUSH   AF   
0282   7C                     LD   A,H   
0283   B5                     OR   L   
0284   C4 7A 02               CALL   NZ,pdec   
0287   F1                     POP   AF   
0288   C6 30                  ADD   A,"0"   
028A   EF                     RST   28h   
028B   C9                     RET      
028C                             ; =============================================================================
028C                             ;  Dispatch table: the low byte of each handler's address, in code order
028C                             ;  (the table itself is the macro PTABLE, defined above the dispatcher).
028C                             ;  It must not cross a page (the dispatcher only adds to its low byte).
028C                             ; =============================================================================
028C                             ; The handlers of the first NPG1 characters start in the image's second page.
028C                             ; ] \ [ @ sit where the two pages meet, and which side each lands on
028C                             ; differs between the builds, so the count is worked out here.
028C                             ; (One division to a line: asm80 only rounds down when it stores a value.)
028C                PGRET:    EQU   (h_ret-BASE)/256   ; 0 = first page, 1 = second
028C                PGBRK:    EQU   (h_break-BASE)/256   
028C                PGDEF:    EQU   (h_def-BASE)/256   
028C                PGFET:    EQU   (h_fetch-BASE)/256   
028C                NPG1:     EQU   21 + PGFET + PGDEF + PGBRK + PGRET   
028C                          IF   1-TABP0   
                    PTAB:        
                              ;*Macro unroll:  PTABLE
                              DB   h_store & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_str & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_num & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_print & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_swap & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_and & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_emit & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_open & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_close & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_mul & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_add & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_cfetch & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_sub & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_cstore & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_div & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_dup & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_drop & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_lt & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_eq & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_gt & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_key & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_fetch & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_def & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_break & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_ret & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_xor & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_alloc & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_grave & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_tor & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_or & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_fromr & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_not & 0FFh   
                    PTABEND:      
028C                          ENDIF      
028C                             ; hexc: if the character at IP is a hex digit (0-9, A-F, a-f), step over it
028C                             ; and return its value in A with the carry set; otherwise leave the IP and
028C                             ; return with the carry clear.
028C   0A           HEXC:     LD   A,(BC)   
028D   D6 30                  SUB   "0"   
028F   FE 0A                  CP   10   
0291   38 09                  JR   C,hc1   
0293   E6 DF                  AND   0DFh   
0295   D6 11                  SUB   11h   
0297   FE 06                  CP   6   
0299   D0                     RET   NC   
029A   D6 F6                  SUB   0F6h   ; + 10, and sets the carry
029C   03           HC1:      INC   BC   
029D   C9                     RET      
029E                             ; =============================================================================
029E                             ;  Console layer. rawk is the host's key routine: a waiting key in A (zero
029E                             ;  flag clear), or A = 0 with the zero flag set when none is waiting. putc
029E                             ;  (RST 28h) prints A. Both keep BC, DE, HL and HL'. In the generic build
029E                             ;  they are the host's KEY and CONOUT routines themselves.
029E                             ; 
029E                             ;  A running program reads the keyboard only through getk and pollk, which
029E                             ;  between them give the break key its rules:
029E                             ;    - Ctrl-C stops the program;
029E                             ;    - any other key that the break check reads is held in KEYBUF for the
029E                             ;      next "?", and a newer one takes its place;
029E                             ;    - "?" (getk) takes the held key first;
029E                             ;    - a program that has stored a non-zero byte at BRKOFF gets Ctrl-C as a
029E                             ;      key like any other, but two of them within about 250 ms still stop it.
029E                             ;  Both are called straight from a handler, never from a routine under one:
029E                             ;  the checked build's report counts on finding one return address above the
029E                             ;  data stack.
029E                             ; =============================================================================
029E                          IFN   CPM   
029E                RAWK:     EQU   KEY   
029E                          ENDIF      
029E                             ; pollk: the break check (see rpushn).
029E   CD 06 FF     POLLK:    CALL   rawk   
02A1   C8                     RET   Z   ; no key
02A2   32 7A 82               LD   (KEYBUF),A   ; held for the next "?"
02A5   FE 03                  CP   3   
02A7   C0                     RET   NZ   
02A8   18 11                  JR   ctlc   
02AA                             ; getk: a key for "?", or A = 0 and the zero flag if there is none.
02AA   E5           GETK:     PUSH   HL   ; a held key goes first, and is taken out of
02AB   21 7A 82               LD   HL,KEYBUF   ;   the buffer
02AE   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   
02AF   36 00                  LD   (HL),0   
02B1   E1                     POP   HL   
02B2   B7                     OR   A   
02B3   C0                     RET   NZ   
02B4   CD 06 FF               CALL   rawk   
02B7   C8                     RET   Z   
02B8   FE 03                  CP   3   
02BA   C0                     RET   NZ   
02BB                             ; ctlc: Ctrl-C has been read. If the break key is on, that is the end. If
02BB                             ; the program has turned it off, wait about 250 ms for one more key: a
02BB                             ; second Ctrl-C is the end too; any other key is held (the newest wins),
02BB                             ; and the Ctrl-C goes to the program: returns A = 3, zero flag clear.
02BB   3A 7B 82     CTLC:     LD   A,(BRKOFF)   
02BE   B7                     OR   A   
02BF   CA 92 03               JP   Z,brk   
02C2   D5                     PUSH   DE   
02C3   11 10 27               LD   DE,250*MSLOOP   
02C6   CD 06 FF     CT1:      CALL   rawk   
02C9   20 05                  JR   NZ,ct2   
02CB   1B                     DEC   DE   
02CC   7A                     LD   A,D   
02CD   B3                     OR   E   
02CE   20 F6                  JR   NZ,ct1   
02D0   D1           CT2:      POP   DE   ; A = the second key, or 0 if none came
02D1   FE 03                  CP   3   
02D3   CA 92 03               JP   Z,brk   
02D6   B7                     OR   A   
02D7   28 03                  JR   Z,ct3   
02D9   32 7A 82               LD   (KEYBUF),A   
02DC   3E 03        CT3:      LD   A,3   
02DE   B7                     OR   A   
02DF   C9                     RET      
02E0                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*(1-EDITOR)   
                    BRK:      EQU   endprog   ; the unchecked build stops without a word
02E0                          ENDIF      ;   (with the editor, both stacks are cleared);
02E0                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*EDITOR   
02E0                BRK:      EQU   edit0   
02E0                          ENDIF      
02E0                          IF   CHECKED   
                    BRK:      EQU   e_break   ;   the checked build reports B
02E0                          ENDIF      
02E0                          IF   CPM   
                    RAWK:     LD   A,0FFh   ; BDOS 6 with E = FFh: a key, or 0
                                 ; putc: BDOS 6 for every character. BDOS 2 would check for ^S while
                                 ; printing and could swallow a key that BDOS 6 then never sees.
                    PUTC:     PUSH   DE   
                              PUSH   HL   
                              LD   E,A   
                              LD   A,6   
                              CALL   bdosx   
                              POP   HL   
                              POP   DE   
                              OR   A   ; (for getk)
                              RET      
                                 ; bdosx: call BDOS function A with DE, keeping BC and HL'
                    BDOSX:    PUSH   BC   
                              EXX      
                              PUSH   HL   
                              EXX      
                              LD   C,A   
                              CALL   BDOS   
                              EXX      
                              POP   HL   
                              EXX      
                              POP   BC   
                              RET      
02E0                          ENDIF      
02E0                             ; =============================================================================
02E0                             ;  Checked build: the checks and the error report
02E0                             ; =============================================================================
02E0                          IF   CHECKED   
                                 ; chkst: stop unless HL is in the program's own space: from the letter page
                                 ; up to the heap limit (the OS, or HEAPLIM), so the interpreter's stacks and
                                 ; whatever lies above the limit are safe. Memory above the heap top but
                                 ; below the limit is the program's own: Tiny BASIC keeps its lines there.
                                 ; It is the page of HL + 1 that is tested, so that one test serves both
                                 ; bytes of a cell: the last byte below the limit can"t be stored to with ".'.
                                 ; Keeps HL and BC.
                    CHKST:    INC   HL   
                              LD   A,H   
                              DEC   HL   
                              CP   LETPAGE   
                              JR   C,chs1   
02E0                          ENDIF      
02E0                          IF   CHECKED*(1-CPM)   
                              CP   HEAPLIM   
                              RET   C   
02E0                          ENDIF      
02E0                          IF   CHECKED*CPM   
                              LD   E,A   
                              LD   A,(0007h)   ; the BDOS page is the heap limit
                              DEC   A   
                              CP   E   
                              RET   NC   
02E0                          ENDIF      
02E0                          IF   CHECKED   
                    CHS1:     JP   e_store   
                                 ; chkhp: HL = the new heap top, DE = the old one, the carry is from adding
                                 ; the count. Stop if the top is not below the limit page, or is below the
                                 ; program's end.
                    CHKHP:       
02E0                          ENDIF      
02E0                          IF   CHECKED*CPM   
                                 ; With this much room a top that wrapped round can land back in
                                 ; range, so the add is tested too: growing (A, the count's high
                                 ; byte, is positive) must not carry, and releasing must.
                              RRA      ; the carry comes in above the sign:
                              ADD   A,40h   ;   bit 7 = carry XOR sign
                              ADD   A,A   
                              JR   C,e_heap   
                              LD   A,(0007h)   
                              DEC   A   
                              CP   H   
                              JR   C,e_heap   
02E0                          ENDIF      
02E0                          IF   CHECKED*(1-CPM)   
                                 ; (Here the program's space is under 32K, so a top that wrapped
                                 ; round always falls outside it.)
                              LD   A,H   
                              CP   HEAPLIM   
                              JR   NC,e_heap   
02E0                          ENDIF      
02E0                          IF   CHECKED   
                              PUSH   DE   
                              EX   DE,HL   
                              LD   HL,(NPEND)   
                              ADD   HL,DE   ; carry: at or above the program's end
                              EX   DE,HL   
                              POP   DE   
                              RET   C   
                    E_HEAP:   OR   A   ; put the count back in TOS for the report
                              SBC   HL,DE   
                              JP   e_heap1   
                                 ; chkstk: both stacks are checked once per character, not in every handler.
                                 ; The data stack is right when SP lies in the 256 bytes below DSTOP: adding
                                 ; the constant carries if it is above (cells were popped that were never
                                 ; pushed), and leaves a high byte of FFh if it is in range. Errors are found
                                 ; a character late at most: the bytes above DSTOP and the guard band below
                                 ; the page take what happens meanwhile. DE is free between characters.
                    CHKSTK:   EX   DE,HL   
                              LD   HL,(1-DSTOP)&0FFFFh   ; (SP is 2 lower here: the call)
                              ADD   HL,SP   
                              EX   DE,HL   
                              JR   C,e_under   
                              INC   D   
                              JR   NZ,e_over   
                              EXX      ; the return stack: in its page (or it has
                              LD   A,H   ;   overflowed), and not above its empty
                              CP   RSPAGE   ;   position (an underflow stays inside the
                              LD   A,L   ;   page, in the guard band)
                              EXX      
                              JR   NZ,e_rover   
                              CP   RSTOP&0FFh+1   
                              RET   C   
                              EXX      ; return stack underflow: it counts as empty
                              LD   HL,RSTOP   
                              EXX      
                              LD   A,"r"   
                              JR   errp   
                    E_ROVER:   LD   A,"R"   ; return stack overflow
                              DB   11h   ; (LD DE,nn hides the next entry)
                    E_OVER:   LD   A,"S"   ; data stack overflow
                              JR   errp   
                    E_UNDER:   LD   SP,DSTOP   ; data stack underflow: it counts as empty
                              LD   A,"s"   
                              JR   error   
                                 ; e_hi: the inner loop read a reserved byte, 80h-FFh: X. But a word cell that
                                 ; was never defined still holds 0000h, and the byte there is a reserved one
                                 ; in every build (AFh or C3h): if the IP is in page zero, this was a call of
                                 ; an undefined word. The call is undone, so the place is the call itself.
                    E_HI:     INC   B   
                              DJNZ   e_resv   ; (B is as it was, and is not 0)
                              RST   08h   
                              LD   B,D   
                              LD   C,E   
                              LD   A,"U"   
                              JR   error   
                                 ; Error entries. Each loads its letter and then hides the next entry inside
                                 ; a 3-byte LD DE,nn (the 11h), so they all fall through to `error`.
                    E_BREAK:   LD   A,"B"   ; Ctrl-C (found inside pollk or getk)
                              DB   11h   
                    E_HEAP1:   LD   A,"H"   ; heap (found inside chkhp)
                              DB   11h   
                    E_STORE:   LD   A,"O"   ; a store outside the program's space (chkst)
                                 ; errp: an error found inside a routine: drop its return address first.
                    ERRP:     POP   DE   
                              JR   error   
                    E_QUOTE:   LD   B,H   ; an unclosed string: HL is its address, one
                              LD   C,L   ;   past the opening quote, which is the place
                              LD   A,"Q"   
                              DB   11h   
                    E_RESV:   LD   A,"X"   ; a reserved byte outside a string
                              DB   11h   
                    E_ZERO:   LD   A,"Z"   ; dividing by zero
                              DB   11h   
                    E_BRACK:   LD   A,"W"   ; bad character after [
                                 ; error: the report, then the end. A = the letter, BC = one past the place,
                                 ; HL = TOS, and both stacks as the report is to show them:
                                 ; 
                                 ;   Err X @ line,col
                                 ;   up to 16 characters of the text from the place
                                 ;   Stk n: the top 8 cells at most, bottom to top
                                 ;   Rtn n
                    ERROR:    PUSH   HL   ; now the whole data stack is in memory
                              LD   E,A   
                              CALL   pnl   
                              DB   "Err ",22h   
                              LD   A,E   
                              RST   28h   
                              CALL   pmsg   
                              DB   " @ ",22h   
                              DEC   BC   ; BC = the place
                                 ; The line and column. A place below the program is in the line
                                 ; buffer: line 0. Otherwise count the LFs from the program's start;
                                 ; DE = the line's number, HL = where it starts.
                              LD   HL,LINEBUF   
                              LD   DE,0   
                              LD   A,B   
                              CP   PROG/256   
                              JR   C,er3   
                              INC   H   
                              LD   L,E   ; HL = PROG
                    ER1:      INC   DE   ; a new line starts at HL
                              PUSH   HL   
                    ER2:      LD   A,L   
                              SUB   C   
                              LD   A,H   
                              SBC   A,B   
                              JR   NC,er2x   ; reached the place
                              LD   A,(HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              CP   10   
                              JR   NZ,er2   
                              POP   AF   
                              JR   er1   
                    ER2X:     POP   HL   
                    ER3:      PUSH   BC   
                              PUSH   HL   
                              EX   DE,HL   
                              CALL   pdec   ; the line
                              LD   A,","   
                              RST   28h   
                              POP   DE   
                              POP   HL   
                              PUSH   HL   
                              OR   A   
                              SBC   HL,DE   
                              INC   HL   
                              CALL   pdec   ; the column
                              CALL   pnl   
                              DB   22h   
                              POP   HL   ; the text, as it is: 16 characters, or fewer
                              LD   B,16   ;   if the line or the program ends first
                    ER4:      LD   A,(HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              OR   A   
                              JR   Z,er5   
                              CP   13   
                              JR   Z,er5   
                              CP   10   
                              JR   Z,er5   
02E0                          ENDIF      
02E0                          IF   CHECKED*CPM   
                              CP   1Ah   ; (the ^Z that pads a file's last record ends
                              JR   Z,er5   ;   the text too: some terminals clear the
02E0                          ENDIF      ;   screen on it)
02E0                          IF   CHECKED   
                              RST   28h   
                              DJNZ   er4   
                    ER5:         ; (without the editor: on into pstk)
02E0                          ENDIF      
02E0                          IF   CHECKED*EDITOR   
                              CALL   pstk   
                              CALL   pnl   
                              DB   22h   
                              JP   edit0   ; back to the editor, with both stacks cleared
02E0                          ENDIF      
02E0                             ; =============================================================================
02E0                             ;  Routines that the checked build's report and the editor share
02E0                             ; =============================================================================
02E0                SPADJ:    EQU   2*EDITOR   ; (with the editor pstk is called, not fallen
02E0                             ;   into: the stack is one address deeper)
02E0                          IF   CHECKED+EDITOR   
02E0                             ; pstk: the two stack lines:  Stk n: the top 8 cells at most, bottom to top
02E0                             ;                             Rtn n
02E0                             ; TOS must be in memory with the rest (pushed). In a build without the
02E0                             ; editor this is the end of `error`, which runs on into it.
02E0   CD 4B 03     PSTK:     CALL   pnl   
02E3   53 74 6B 20 22         DB   "Stk ",22h   
02E8   21 F8 81               LD   HL,DSTOP-2-SPADJ   ; (the cell at DSTOP-2 was pushed with the
02EB   B7                     OR   A   ;   first value and holds nothing)
02EC   ED 72                  SBC   HL,SP   
02EE   CD 31 03               CALL   phalf   ; the depth
02F1   3E 3A                  LD   A,":"   
02F3   EF                     RST   28h   
02F4   79                     LD   A,C   
02F5   FE 09                  CP   9   
02F7   38 0A                  JR   C,er6   
02F9   CD 51 03               CALL   pmsg   
02FC   20 2E 2E 2E 22         DB   " ...",22h   
0301   0E 08                  LD   C,8   
0303   26 00        ER6:      LD   H,0   ; C = the number of cells to show
0305   69                     LD   L,C   
0306   29                     ADD   HL,HL   
0307   39                     ADD   HL,SP   ; HL -> just above the deepest of them
0308                          ENDIF      
0308                          IF   EDITOR   
0308   23                     INC   HL   
0309   23                     INC   HL   
030A                          ENDIF      
030A                          IF   CHECKED+EDITOR   
030A   0C                     INC   C   
030B   0D           ER7:      DEC   C   
030C   28 11                  JR   Z,er8   
030E   2B                     DEC   HL   
030F   56                     LD   D,(HL)   
0310   2B                     DEC   HL   
0311   5E                     LD   E,(HL)   
0312   E5                     PUSH   HL   
0313   C5                     PUSH   BC   
0314   3E 20                  LD   A," "   
0316   EF                     RST   28h   
0317   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
0318   CD 72 02               CALL   psgn   
031B   C1                     POP   BC   
031C   E1                     POP   HL   
031D   18 EC                  JR   er7   
031F   CD 4B 03     ER8:      CALL   pnl   
0322   52 74 6E 20 22         DB   "Rtn ",22h   
0327   D9                     EXX      
0328   E5                     PUSH   HL   
0329   D9                     EXX      
032A   D1                     POP   DE   
032B   21 E0 80               LD   HL,RSTOP   
032E   B7                     OR   A   
032F   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   
0331                          ENDIF      
0331                          IF   CHECKED*(1-EDITOR)   
                              CALL   phalf   
                              CALL   pnl   
                              DB   22h   
                              JP   endprog   
0331                          ENDIF      
0331                          IF   CHECKED+EDITOR   
0331                             ; phalf: print half of HL, and leave it in C. (With the editor, pstk ends by
0331                             ; running on into this.)
0331   CB 3C        PHALF:    SRL   H   
0333   CB 1D                  RR   L   
0335   E5                     PUSH   HL   
0336   CD 7A 02               CALL   pdec   
0339   C1                     POP   BC   
033A   C9                     RET      
033B                             ; prstr: print the string at HL, to its closing quote, decoding "/" (this is
033B                             ; "$", and the texts of the report and the editor). In the checked build a
033B                             ; NUL first is an error: Q.
033B   7E           PRSTR:    LD   A,(HL)   
033C   23                     INC   HL   
033D   FE 22                  CP   22h   
033F   C8                     RET   Z   
0340                          ENDIF      
0340                          IF   CHECKED   
                              OR   A   
                              JR   Z,e_dollar   
0340                          ENDIF      
0340                          IF   CHECKED+EDITOR   
0340   FE 2F                  CP   "/"   
0342   20 04                  JR   NZ,prs1   
0344   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   
0345   23                     INC   HL   
0346   E6 BF                  AND   0BFh   
0348   EF           PRS1:     RST   28h   
0349   18 F0                  JR   prstr   
034B                             ; pmsg: print the text that follows the CALL, to its closing quote. Keeps HL.
034B                             ; pnl: the same, on a new line.
034B   3E 0D        PNL:      LD   A,13   
034D   EF                     RST   28h   
034E   3E 0A                  LD   A,10   
0350   EF                     RST   28h   
0351   E3           PMSG:     EX   (SP),HL   
0352   CD 3B 03               CALL   prstr   
0355   E3                     EX   (SP),HL   
0356   C9                     RET      
0357                          ENDIF      
0357                          IF   CHECKED   
                    E_DOLLAR:   POP   DE   ; "$" ran into a NUL: drop the return address,
                              POP   HL   ;   and put the string's address back in TOS
                              LD   A,"Q"   
                              JP   error   
0357                          ENDIF      
0357                             ; =============================================================================
0357                             ;  The line editor (EDITOR = 1)
0357                             ; 
0357                             ;  The interpreter starts here, and a program that ends comes back here.
0357                             ;  There is no prompt. It follows the spec's suggested standard for a line
0357                             ;  editor (docs/b8script.md, Environments). Type a line and press Return:
0357                             ; 
0357                             ;    n text    put the text in as line n; the lines from n on move down. A
0357                             ;              number past the end (or 0) adds the line at the end.
0357                             ;    n         take line n out
0357                             ;    anything else is run at once, as B8Script. (Start such a line with a
0357                             ;    space if it would begin with a digit.)
0357                             ; 
0357                             ;  A command key ends the line too, and takes what was typed as its argument:
0357                             ; 
0357                             ;    ^G        run the program
0357                             ;    n ^L      list from line n (no number: all of it). Any key holds the
0357                             ;              list until another key is pressed; Ctrl-C ends it.
0357                             ;    n ^E      put line n in the input line; Return puts it back, changed
0357                             ;    name ^R   read. CP/M: the file of that name (no name: the same file as
0357                             ;              last time). Generic: what is typed, or pasted, from now until
0357                             ;              ^Z replaces the program; it is not echoed.
0357                             ;    name ^W   write. CP/M: to that file (no name: the same file as last
0357                             ;              time). Generic: the text is printed, as it is.
0357                             ;    ^N ^N     new: no program (the key twice in a row)
0357                             ;    ^V        view: the build, both stacks, and the program's size, lines
0357                             ;              and free memory
0357                             ;    ^X        leave (to LEAVE)
0357                             ; 
0357                             ;  In the line: ^B and ^F, or the left and right arrow keys, move the cursor;
0357                             ;  a character goes in at the cursor; Backspace and DEL take out the one
0357                             ;  before it; Esc drops the line. Only CR, LF, BS and printing characters are
0357                             ;  sent to the terminal, so any terminal will do.
0357                             ; 
0357                             ;  Lines are counted, not numbered: the text holds no line numbers, and the
0357                             ;  list shows each line's place. There can be 65535 lines. A typed line holds
0357                             ;  125 characters; the one character after a line number separates it from
0357                             ;  the text and is not stored. The text is kept as it is typed, each line
0357                             ;  ending in CR LF, at PROG.
0357                             ; 
0357                             ;  What lasts from one line to the next: the program, the words, the
0357                             ;  variables and the data stack. An error or a break clears both stacks. The
0357                             ;  return stack starts empty for every line.
0357                             ; 
0357                             ;  Things to know:
0357                             ;    - Reset empties the program (generic builds).
0357                             ;    - A word's address points into the program, so run the program again
0357                             ;      after editing it.
0357                             ;    - Nothing is printed between a program's output and what is typed next.
0357                             ;    - A line run at once sits in the line buffer, which -n? also reads into:
0357                             ;      a line that calls -n? and carries on afterwards runs what was typed.
0357                             ;      (The stored program never comes back to the line, so it may.)
0357                             ;    - The editor"s own keys are not the program"s: -n? is the plain line
0357                             ;      read of the other builds (BDOS 10 under CP/M).
0357                             ; 
0357                             ;  The data stack is the CPU's stack, so the editor works on top of whatever
0357                             ;  the last line left there, with TOS pushed like the rest.
0357                             ; =============================================================================
0357                          IF   EDGEN   
0357                INIT:        ; reset (A = 0)
0357                          ENDIF      
0357                          IF   EDGEN*CHECKED   
                                 ; Clear the lower half of the letter page: every variable starts at 0, and
                                 ; every word cell holds 0000h, the address an undefined word is caught at
                                 ; (see e_hi).
                              LD   HL,LET   
                    INI1:     LD   (HL),A   
                              INC   L   
                              JP   P,ini1   ; +00h to +7Fh
0357                          ENDIF      
0357                          IF   EDGEN   
0357   18 39                  JR   edit0   
0359                          ENDIF      
0359                          IF   EDITOR   
0359                             ; ^B, left arrow: the cursor goes one to the left
0359   7D           LEFT:     LD   A,L   
035A   87                     ADD   A,A   
035B   28 4D                  JR   Z,ed1   ; (L = 80h: at the start)
035D   2D                     DEC   L   
035E   3E 08                  LD   A,8   
0360   EF           LF1:      RST   28h   
0361   18 47                  JR   ed1   
0363                             ; ^F, right arrow: one to the right, by printing the character there
0363   7D           RIGHT:    LD   A,L   
0364   BB                     CP   E   
0365   28 43                  JR   Z,ed1   ; at the end
0367   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   
0368   2C                     INC   L   
0369   18 F5                  JR   lf1   
036B                             ; Esc: alone it drops the line. An arrow key sends Esc [ and a letter, so
036B                             ; wait about 5 ms for a second key: after a "[" read on to the letter that
036B                             ; ends the sequence, and act on C (right) and D (left).
036B   01 C8 00     ESC:      LD   BC,5*MSLOOP   
036E   CD 06 FF     ES1:      CALL   rawk   
0371   20 0A                  JR   NZ,es2   
0373   0B                     DEC   BC   
0374   78                     LD   A,B   
0375   B1                     OR   C   
0376   20 F6                  JR   NZ,es1   
0378   CD DF 03               CALL   fin   ; no second key: the line is dropped
037B   18 1B                  JR   edit   
037D   FE 5B        ES2:      CP   "["   
037F   20 29                  JR   NZ,ed1   ; not a sequence known here
0381   CD 38 04     ES3:      CALL   ekey   
0384   FE 40                  CP   40h   
0386   38 F9                  JR   C,es3   ; (its parameters)
0388   FE 43                  CP   "C"   
038A   28 D7                  JR   Z,right   
038C   FE 44                  CP   "D"   
038E   28 C9                  JR   Z,left   
0390   18 18                  JR   ed1   
0392                             ; edit0: reset, an error or a break: both stacks are cleared.
0392                             ; skend: a program that ended inside skip: its return address goes.
0392                             ; edend: a program that ended: TOS joins the rest of the data stack.
0392   31 FA 81     EDIT0:    LD   SP,DSTOP-2   ; empty (the cell that stands for TOS is pushed)
0395   21                     DB   21h   ; (LD HL,nn: steps over the next two bytes)
0396   D1           SKEND:    POP   DE   
0397   E5           EDEND:    PUSH   HL   
0398                             ; edit: start a new input line.
0398   D9           EDIT:     EXX      
0399   21 E0 80               LD   HL,RSTOP   ; the return stack is empty
039C   D9                     EXX      
039D   21 00 00               LD   HL,0   
03A0   22 7A 82               LD   (KEYBUF),HL   ; no key is held, and the break key is on
03A3   22 3A 82               LD   (EDLN),HL   ; no line is being edited
03A6   21 80 82               LD   HL,LINEBUF   ; HL = the cursor,
03A9   5D                     LD   E,L   ;   E = the end of the line (its low byte)
03AA   CD 38 04     ED1:      CALL   ekey   
03AD   FE 7F                  CP   7Fh   
03AF   28 40                  JR   Z,bsp   ; DEL
03B1   FE 20                  CP   " "   
03B3   30 56                  JR   NC,insc   
03B5   FE 09                  CP   9   
03B7   28 52                  JR   Z,insc   ; Tab is text
03B9   FE 08                  CP   8   
03BB   28 34                  JR   Z,bsp   
03BD   FE 02                  CP   2   
03BF   28 98                  JR   Z,left   ; ^B
03C1   FE 06                  CP   6   
03C3   28 9E                  JR   Z,right   ; ^F
03C5   FE 1B                  CP   1Bh   
03C7   28 A2                  JR   Z,esc   
03C9   E5                     PUSH   HL   ; a command key? Look it up
03CA   21 3E 04               LD   HL,cmds   
03CD   06 09                  LD   B,NCMD   
03CF   BE           ED2:      CP   (HL)   
03D0   23                     INC   HL   
03D1   28 07                  JR   Z,ed3   
03D3   23                     INC   HL   
03D4   23                     INC   HL   
03D5   10 F8                  DJNZ   ed2   
03D7   E1                     POP   HL   
03D8   18 D0                  JR   ed1   ; no: the key is ignored
03DA   7E           ED3:      LD   A,(HL)   
03DB   23                     INC   HL   
03DC   66                     LD   H,(HL)   
03DD   6F                     LD   L,A   
03DE   E3                     EX   (SP),HL   ; the command's address: fin returns to it
03DF                             ; fin: end the input line: CR LF and a NUL after it, and a new line on the
03DF                             ; terminal. Leaves BC -> the line and HL -> the NUL.
03DF   26 82        FIN:      LD   H,LETPAGE   
03E1   6B                     LD   L,E   
03E2   36 0D                  LD   (HL),13   
03E4   2C                     INC   L   
03E5   36 0A                  LD   (HL),10   
03E7   2D                     DEC   L   
03E8   CD B1 05               CALL   prl   ; (prints the CR LF)
03EB   36 00                  LD   (HL),0   
03ED   01 80 82               LD   BC,LINEBUF   
03F0   C9                     RET      
03F1                             ; Backspace, DEL: the character before the cursor goes. The cursor moves
03F1                             ; left, the rest of the line moves down over it, and the last place (now a
03F1                             ; space) is printed over along with the rest.
03F1   7D           BSP:      LD   A,L   
03F2   87                     ADD   A,A   
03F3   28 B5                  JR   Z,ed1   ; at the start
03F5   2D                     DEC   L   
03F6   3E 08                  LD   A,8   
03F8   EF                     RST   28h   
03F9   E5                     PUSH   HL   
03FA   2C           BS1:      INC   L   
03FB   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   
03FC   2D                     DEC   L   
03FD   77                     LD   (HL),A   
03FE   2C                     INC   L   
03FF   7D                     LD   A,L   
0400   BB                     CP   E   
0401   20 F7                  JR   NZ,bs1   
0403   2D                     DEC   L   
0404   36 20                  LD   (HL)," "   
0406   E1                     POP   HL   
0407   53                     LD   D,E   
0408   1D                     DEC   E   
0409   18 15                  JR   ic2   
040B                             ; A character goes in at the cursor: it ripples up through the rest of the
040B                             ; line, the cursor moves on, and the rest is printed again.
040B   47           INSC:     LD   B,A   
040C   7B                     LD   A,E   
040D   FE FD                  CP   0FDh   
040F   28 99                  JR   Z,ed1   ; the line is full: 125 characters
0411   78                     LD   A,B   
0412   EF                     RST   28h   
0413   E5                     PUSH   HL   
0414   7E           IC1:      LD   A,(HL)   
0415   70                     LD   (HL),B   
0416   47                     LD   B,A   
0417   7D                     LD   A,L   
0418   2C                     INC   L   
0419   BB                     CP   E   
041A   20 F8                  JR   NZ,ic1   
041C   E1                     POP   HL   
041D   2C                     INC   L   
041E   1C                     INC   E   
041F   53                     LD   D,E   
0420   CD 25 04     IC2:      CALL   tail   
0423   18 85                  JR   ed1   
0425                             ; tail: print the line from the cursor to D (a low byte), and bring the
0425                             ; cursor back with backspaces. Nothing at all if the cursor is at D.
0425   4D           TAIL:     LD   C,L   
0426   7D           TA1:      LD   A,L   
0427   BA                     CP   D   
0428   28 05                  JR   Z,ta2   
042A   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   
042B   EF                     RST   28h   
042C   2C                     INC   L   
042D   18 F7                  JR   ta1   
042F   7D           TA2:      LD   A,L   
0430   B9                     CP   C   
0431   C8                     RET   Z   
0432   3E 08                  LD   A,8   
0434   EF                     RST   28h   
0435   2D                     DEC   L   
0436   18 F7                  JR   ta2   
0438                             ; ekey: wait for a key
0438   CD 06 FF     EKEY:     CALL   rawk   
043B   28 FB                  JR   Z,ekey   
043D   C9                     RET      
043E                             ; The command keys, and where each goes (after fin).
043E   0D           CMDS:     DB   13   
043F   98 04                  DW   cret   
0441   07                     DB   7   ; ^G
0442   E0 04                  DW   crun   
0444   0C                     DB   12   ; ^L
0445   F2 04                  DW   clist   
0447   05                     DB   5   ; ^E
0448   67 04                  DW   cedln   
044A   12                     DB   18   ; ^R
044B   BA 05                  DW   cread   
044D   17                     DB   23   ; ^W
044E   ED 05                  DW   cwrite   
0450   0E                     DB   14   ; ^N
0451   59 04                  DW   cnew   
0453   16                     DB   22   ; ^V
0454   24 05                  DW   cview   
0456   18                     DB   24   ; ^X
0457   09 FF                  DW   LEAVE   
0459                NCMD:     EQU   9   
0459                             ; ^N ^N: no program, if the next key is ^N too
0459   CD 38 04     CNEW:     CALL   ekey   
045C   FE 0E                  CP   14   
045E   20 04                  JR   NZ,ged0   
0460   AF                     XOR   A   
0461   32 00 83               LD   (PROG),A   
0464   C3 98 03     GED0:     JP   edit   
0467                             ; ^E: line n goes into the input line, to be changed. EDLN remembers which
0467                             ; line it was: Return puts the text back in its place.
0467   CD 2F 02     CEDLN:    CALL   rdnum   
046A   E5                     PUSH   HL   
046B   CD 99 05               CALL   find   ; HL -> the line, or the NUL if there is none
046E   D1                     POP   DE   
046F   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   
0470   B7                     OR   A   
0471   28 F1                  JR   Z,ged0   
0473   ED 53 3A 82            LD   (EDLN),DE   
0477   11 80 82               LD   DE,LINEBUF   
047A   7E           CE1:      LD   A,(HL)   
047B   FE 0D                  CP   13   
047D   28 0C                  JR   Z,ce2   
047F   FE 0A                  CP   10   
0481   28 08                  JR   Z,ce2   
0483   12                     LD   (DE),A   
0484   23                     INC   HL   
0485   1C                     INC   E   
0486   7B                     LD   A,E   
0487   FE FD                  CP   0FDh   ; (a longer line is cut at 125 characters)
0489   20 EF                  JR   NZ,ce1   
048B   21 80 82     CE2:      LD   HL,LINEBUF   ; show it; the cursor ends up at its end
048E   7D           CE3:      LD   A,L   
048F   BB                     CP   E   
0490   CA AA 03               JP   Z,ed1   
0493   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   
0494   EF                     RST   28h   
0495   2C                     INC   L   
0496   18 F6                  JR   ce3   
0498                             ; Return. If ^E put a line here, the text goes back in its place. If not:
0498                             ; a number and text is a line to put in, a number alone a line to take out,
0498                             ; and anything else is run where it is.
0498   E5           CRET:     PUSH   HL   ; the end of what was typed
0499   2A 3A 82               LD   HL,(EDLN)   
049C   7C                     LD   A,H   
049D   B5                     OR   L   
049E   28 07                  JR   Z,cr1   
04A0   E5                     PUSH   HL   
04A1   CD 89 05               CALL   delln   
04A4   E1                     POP   HL   
04A5   18 13                  JR   ins   
04A7   CD 2F 02     CR1:      CALL   rdnum   ; HL = the number it starts with, BC -> after
04AA   79                     LD   A,C   ; C is still 80h if there was no number:
04AB   87                     ADD   A,A   ;   only then is twice it 0
04AC   28 36                  JR   Z,st0p   ; no number: run the line
04AE   0A                     LD   A,(BC)   
04AF   FE 0D                  CP   13   
04B1   20 06                  JR   NZ,cr2   
04B3   D1                     POP   DE   ; the number alone: take that line out
04B4   CD 89 05               CALL   delln   
04B7   18 24                  JR   gedit   
04B9   03           CR2:      INC   BC   ; step over the one character after the number
04BA                             ; Put the text at BC in as line n (in HL): open a gap of its length there,
04BA                             ; CR and LF included, and copy it in.
04BA   CD 99 05     INS:      CALL   find   ; HL -> where it goes
04BD   D1                     POP   DE   ; the end of what was typed
04BE   7B                     LD   A,E   
04BF   91                     SUB   C   ; A = the length of the text, with its CR LF
04C0   C5                     PUSH   BC   ; the text
04C1   4F                     LD   C,A   
04C2   06 00                  LD   B,0   
04C4   C5                     PUSH   BC   ; its length
04C5   54                     LD   D,H   
04C6   5D                     LD   E,L   ; DE = where it goes
04C7   AF                     XOR   A   
04C8   4F                     LD   C,A   ; BC = 0: CPIR looks as far as it needs to
04C9   ED B1                  CPIR      ; HL -> one past the program's NUL
04CB   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   ; the number of bytes to move up, NUL included
04CD   44                     LD   B,H   
04CE   4D                     LD   C,L   
04CF   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
04D0   2B                     DEC   HL   ; HL -> the NUL
04D1   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
04D2   E3                     EX   (SP),HL   ; HL = the length; where it goes is kept
04D3   E5                     PUSH   HL   
04D4   19                     ADD   HL,DE   ; the NUL's new place
04D5   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
04D6   ED B8                  LDDR      ; move the rest of the program up
04D8   C1                     POP   BC   ; the length
04D9   D1                     POP   DE   ; where it goes
04DA   E1                     POP   HL   ; the text
04DB   ED B0                  LDIR      
04DD   C3 98 03     GEDIT:    JP   edit   
04E0                             ; ^G: run the program. st0p: run the typed line (BC -> it).
04E0   01 00 83     CRUN:     LD   BC,PROG   
04E3   3E                     DB   3Eh   ; (LD A,n: steps over the POP)
04E4   E1           ST0P:     POP   HL   ; (the end of what was typed)
04E5                             ; st0: start running at BC. The heap starts after the stored program's NUL.
04E5   21 00 83     ST0:      LD   HL,PROG   
04E8   AF                     XOR   A   
04E9   BE           ST1:      CP   (HL)   
04EA   23                     INC   HL   
04EB   20 FC                  JR   NZ,st1   
04ED   22 7C 82               LD   (HEAP),HL   
04F0                          ENDIF      
04F0                          IF   EDITOR*CHECKED   
                              RST   20h   ; minus the heap"s first address: "_' may not
                              LD   (NPEND),HL   ;   release below it
04F0                          ENDIF      
04F0                          IF   EDITOR   
04F0   E1                     POP   HL   ; TOS: the data stack is as the last line left it
04F1   F7                     RST   30h   ; (its return address is thrown away)
04F2                             ; ^L: list from line n. DE = the number of the line at HL.
04F2   CD 2F 02     CLIST:    CALL   rdnum   ; HL = n, or 0 if there was none:
04F5   7C                     LD   A,H   
04F6   B5                     OR   L   
04F7   20 01                  JR   NZ,li0   
04F9   2C                     INC   L   ;   then from line 1
04FA   E5           LI0:      PUSH   HL   
04FB   CD 99 05               CALL   find   
04FE   D1                     POP   DE   
04FF   7E           LI1:      LD   A,(HL)   
0500   B7                     OR   A   
0501   28 DA                  JR   Z,gedit   ; the end of the text
0503   CD 06 FF               CALL   rawk   
0506   28 0B                  JR   Z,li3   ; no key: carry on
0508   FE 03                  CP   3   
050A   28 D1                  JR   Z,gedit   ; Ctrl-C
050C   CD 38 04               CALL   ekey   ; any other key: wait for one more
050F   FE 03                  CP   3   
0511   28 CA                  JR   Z,gedit   
0513   E5           LI3:      PUSH   HL   
0514   D5                     PUSH   DE   
0515   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
0516   CD 7A 02               CALL   pdec   ; the line's number,
0519   3E 20                  LD   A," "   
051B   EF                     RST   28h   ;   a space,
051C   D1                     POP   DE   
051D   E1                     POP   HL   
051E   13                     INC   DE   
051F   CD B1 05               CALL   prl   ;   and the line
0522   18 DB                  JR   li1   
0524                             ; ^V: view.
0524   CD 51 03     CVIEW:    CALL   pmsg   
0527   42 38 53 5A 38 30 45   DB   "B8SZ80E"   
052E                          ENDIF      
